Change:
  Runtime resource validation now requires usable filesystem bytes to cover
  the declared physical disk safety watermark, checkpoint-restore temporary
  headroom, and compaction temporary headroom. Startup envelope validation
  already constrains their checked sum to maxFilesystemBytes.

Focused regression:
  WorkerResourceEnvelopeTest.runtimeFilesystemMustRetainSafetyWatermarkAndTemporaryHeadroom
  With 2 GiB watermark and 256 MiB for each temporary bucket, exactly 2.5 GiB
  usable space is accepted and 2.5 GiB minus 1 byte is rejected.

